# Real job files for headless use hold archivist names and paths to
# client material, so they never enter the repo. Name them
# <name>.job.json. Only job.example.json (placeholder values) is
# committed; it does not match these patterns.
job.json
*.job.json

# Written by a run of the example job (output/) and by the GUI (the log
# file, which holds source paths). This repo's root .gitignore covers both
# as well; these lines matter in the public copy.
output/
*.log
